{
  "title": "88: al-Ghaasheyah الغاشية",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ الْغَاشِيَةِؕ‏(1)\nHAL ATAAKA HADEESUL GHAASHEYAH.\nHath not come unto thee the tidings of the Overwhelming Event?\nوُجُوْهٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ خَاشِعَةٌ ۙ‏(2)\nWOJOOHUN-Y YAWMA-EZIN KHAASHE-A’TUN.\n(Some) faces on that day shall be downcast\nعَامِلَةٌ نَّاصِبَةٌ ۙ‏(3)\nA’AMELATUN NAASEBATUN.\nToiling, weary\nتَصْلٰى نَارًا حَامِيَةً ۙ‏(4)\nTASLAA NAARAN HAAME-YATAN.\nEntering into the fire, blazing\nتُسْقٰى مِنْ عَيْنٍ اٰنِيَةٍؕ‏(5)\nTUSQAA MIN A’YNIN AANEYAH.\nMade to drink from a spring (fiercely) boiling\nلَيْسَ لَهُمْ طَعَامٌ اِلَّا مِنْ ضَرِيْعٍۙ‏(6)\nLAYSAA LAHUM TA-A’AMUN ILLAA MIN ZAREE-I’L.\nFor them there shall not be (any) food but of the bitter-thorny fruit ‘Zaree\nلَّا يُسْمِنُ وَلَا يُغْنِىْ مِنْ جُوْعٍؕ‏(7)\nLAA YUSMENO WA LAA YUGHNEE MIN JOO’.\nWhich will neither fatten nor give any relief from hunger\nوُجُوْهٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ نَّاعِمَةٌ ۙ‏(8)\nWOJOOHUN-Y YAWMA-EZIN NAA-E’MAUL.\n(Other) faces on that day shall be happy\nلِّسَعْيِهَا رَاضِيَةٌ ۙ‏(9)\nLE-SA’YEHAA RAAZEYATUN.\nWith their efforts past, well pleased\nفِىْ جَنَّةٍ عَالِيَةٍۙ‏(10)\nFEE JANNATIN A’ALEYATIL.\nIn a grand garden\nلَّا تَسْمَعُ فِيْهَا لَاغِيَةً ؕ‏(11)\nLAA TASMA-O’ FEEHAL LAAGHEYAH.\nThey shall hear not therein any vain talk\nفِيْهَا عَيْنٌ جَارِيَةٌ‌ ۘ‏(12)\nFEEHAA A’YNUN JAAREYAH.\nTherein a spring flowing\nفِيْهَا سُرُرٌ مَّرْفُوْعَةٌ ۙ‏(13)\nFEEHAA SORORUM MAR-FOO-A’TUNW.\nTherein are couches exalted\nوَّاَكْوَابٌ مَّوْضُوْعَةٌ ۙ‏(14)\nWA AKWAABUM MAW-ZOO-A’TUNW.\nAnd goblets ready placed\nوَّنَمَارِقُ مَصْفُوْفَةٌ ۙ‏(15)\nWA NAMAAREQO MASFOOAFUNW.\nAnd cushions ranged in order\nوَّزَرَابِىُّ مَبْثُوْثَةٌ ؕ‏(16)\nWA ZARAABIYYO MABSOOSAH.\nAnd carpets spread forth\nاَفَلَا يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَى الْاِ بِلِ كَيْفَ خُلِقَتْ‏(17)\nAFALAA YANZOROONA ELAL EBELE KAYFA KHOLEQAT.\nWhat! See they not unto the camels, how they are created?\nوَاِلَى السَّمَآءِ كَيْفَ رُفِعَتْ‏(18)\nWA ELAS SAMAAA-E KAYFA RO-FE-A’T.\nAnd Unto the heaven, how it is raised\nوَاِلَى الْجِبَالِ كَيْفَ نُصِبَتْ‏(19)\nWA ELAL JEBAALE KAYFA NOSEBAT.\nAnd unto the mountains, how they are set up?\nوَاِلَى الْاَرْضِ كَيْفَ سُطِحَتْ‏(20)\nWA ELAL ARZE KAYFA SOTEHAT.\nAnd unto the earth, how it is spread out?\nفَذَكِّرْ ؕ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مُذَكِّرٌ ؕ‏(21)\nFAZAKKIR, INNAMAA ANTA MOZAKKER.\nSo, thou (go on) reminding; Thou art only a Reminder\nلَسْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِمُصَۜيْطِرٍۙ‏(22)\nLASTA A’LAYHIM BE-MOSAYTERIN.\nThou art not, over them, a compeller\nاِلَّا مَنْ تَوَلّٰى وَكَفَرَۙ‏(23)\nILLAA MAN TAWALLAA WA KAFARA.\nBut whosoever turneth back and disbelieveth\nفَيُعَذِّبُهُ اللّٰهُ الْعَذَابَ الْاَكْبَرَؕ‏(24)\nFA-YO-A’ZZEBOHUL LAAHUL A’ZAABAL AKBAR.\nThen will chastise him God with the greatest chastisement\nاِنَّ اِلَيْنَاۤ اِيَابَهُمْۙ‏(25)\nINNA ELAYNAA EYAABAHUM.\nVerily unto Us is their return\nثُمَّ اِنَّ عَلَيْنَا حِسَابَهُمْ‏(26)\nSUMMA INNA A’LAYNAA HESAABAHUM.\nThen verily, upon Us is to reckon with them",
  "merits": "Surah al-Ghaasheyah (The Overwhelming Calamity)\nThis is a ‘Makki’ Surah and it has 26 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the one who recites this Surah will not face difficulty in the accounting of deeds on the Day of Judgement and Allah (s.w.t.) will show Mercy to him and save him from Hell.\nReciting this Surah near a baby removes fright from him and stops his crying. Imam Ali (a.s.) has said that if this Surah is recited over a part of the body which is paining, the pain will go away and if recited over food items, it removes any bad effects of that food."
